 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon MemoryDB API (2021-01-01). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Parameter groups, subnet groups and IAM-authenticated users are stored configuration: no cluster, shard, node, snapshot, ACL or multi-Region cluster exists, and CreateCluster, CreateACL, CreateSnapshot and the other data-plane APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. Users must use iam authentication; password authentication is refused so no password is stored. The default user, default parameter groups and the open-access ACL are not pre-created, and parameter values (DescribeParameters, UpdateParameterGroup, ResetParameterGroup) are not implemented. Parameter group families, subnet IDs and access strings are stored without validation; subnet groups report no VPC or Availability Zone. Describe filters by name return an empty list for an unknown name instead of a not-found fault, and the Filters member is refused. TagResource and UntagResource return no TagList, and removing a missing tag key succeeds.",
  "title": "Amazon MemoryDB (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2021-01-01"
 },
 "openapi": "3.1.0",
